---
import Layout from '@/components/Layout.astro';
import PageHeader from '@/components/PageHeader.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy — Earthsong"
  description="How Earthsong limits data collection, uses its hosting provider, handles external links, and responds to privacy questions."
>
  <PageHeader
    eyebrow="Policy · Effective August 6, 2026"
    title="Privacy begins with restraint"
    description="Earthsong is designed to be read without being watched. This policy names what the site does, what its infrastructure necessarily processes, and what it does not collect."
  />

  <article class="policy-prose prose prose-lg mt-12 max-w-3xl prose-earthsong">
    <aside class="not-prose rounded-lg border border-moss/20 bg-white/60 p-6 shadow-field sm:p-8" aria-labelledby="privacy-short-version">
      <p class="font-mono text-[10px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-ember-dark">The short version</p>
      <h2 id="privacy-short-version" class="policy-card-title mt-3 font-display text-4xl uppercase tracking-[0.05em] text-ink">No analytics. No tracking cookies. No profiles.</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 font-body text-sm leading-[1.8] text-stone">
        Earthsong does not sell personal information, run advertising technology, or ask visitors to create accounts. The current site does not collect newsletter addresses. Standard web requests are processed by our host so the pages can be delivered securely.
      </p>
    </aside>

    <h2>Our standard</h2>

    <p>
      This policy follows two principles: contextual integrity and privacy by design.
    </p>

    <h3>Contextual integrity</h3>

    <p>
      Information should move only in ways appropriate to the context that produced it. Reading an Earthsong page should not quietly become an advertising profile, a mailing-list entry, or a sale to someone else.
    </p>

    <h3>Privacy by design</h3>

    <p>
      Privacy works best as the default. Earthsong limits collection before data exists, serves fonts and images from its own site, and does not add analytics or tracking tools simply because they are available.
    </p>

    <h2>This site</h2>

    <p>
      This is the operational privacy policy for earthsong.io. It covers the public pages, seasonal letters, downloadable calendar, and the links provided by this site. It does not cover any other site reached through an external link; the destination's own policies apply once you leave Earthsong.
    </p>

    <h3>What Earthsong collects</h3>

    <p>
      Earthsong itself collects no information that you type into the site. There are no accounts, comments, purchases, surveys, active newsletter forms, or contact forms. We do not use analytics, advertising pixels, session replay, fingerprinting, or social-media trackers.
    </p>

    <h3>What the hosting infrastructure processes</h3>

    <p>
      Earthsong is hosted by Vercel. Like any web host, Vercel must process a request when your browser asks for a page or file. That request may include an IP address, browser and device information, the requested address, and a date and time. This information is used to deliver and protect the site. Earthsong does not combine it into visitor profiles or use it to measure individual behavior.
    </p>

    <p>
      Infrastructure handling and retention are governed by <a href="https://vercel.com/legal/privacy-policy">Vercel's privacy policy</a> and the service configuration in effect at the time of a request.
    </p>

    <h3>Cookies and browser storage</h3>

    <p>
      Earthsong sets no cookies and writes nothing to local storage or session storage. It does not need a cookie banner because it does not use those technologies. An external site linked from Earthsong may make different choices.
    </p>

    <h3>Seasonal-letter subscriptions</h3>

    <p>
      The current site offers a public letter archive and does not transmit email addresses. If a subscription service is enabled later, Earthsong will identify the provider and update this policy before collection begins. The form will explain where an address goes before a reader submits it.
    </p>

    <h3>Calendar downloads</h3>

    <p>
      Downloading or subscribing to the Earthsong calendar requests a public <code>.ics</code> file from the host. Earthsong does not receive the contents of your calendar, learn whether you imported the file, or place events anywhere without your calendar application's action.
    </p>

    <h3>External links</h3>

    <p>
      Letters cite scientific, historical, governmental, and cultural sources. Following one of those links sends a normal request to that organization. Earthsong does not control the destination's accessibility, cookies, or privacy practices.
    </p>

    <h2>Choices and rights</h2>

    <p>
      Because Earthsong does not maintain visitor accounts, receive form submissions, or operate a subscriber database, it will usually have no personal record to retrieve, correct, export, or delete. Requests concerning information processed by the hosting infrastructure should be directed to Vercel under its privacy policy.
    </p>

    <h3>Children</h3>

    <p>
      Earthsong is a general-audience reading site and does not knowingly collect personal information from children. If you believe a child has provided personal information through one of the linked services, contact us so the appropriate service can be identified and the request addressed.
    </p>

    <h3>Changes</h3>

    <p>
      Meaningful changes will be dated on this page and will not be applied retroactively. If Earthsong begins collecting information directly, the policy will be updated before that collection starts.
    </p>

    <h3>Maintenance</h3>

    <p>
      Earthsong is maintained as an independent public project. This policy is reviewed whenever the site's collection practices, infrastructure, or public features materially change.
    </p>

    <hr />

    <p><strong>Effective and last reviewed:</strong> August 6, 2026.</p>
  </article>
</Layout>
